---
export const title = 'Placement';
export const order = 350;
---
<p>
  <code>placement</code> sets where the menu opens relative to its anchor: a side, <code>top</code>,
  <code>bottom</code>, <code>start</code> or <code>end</code>, optionally followed by an alignment,
  <code>-start</code> or <code>-end</code>. The default is <code>bottom-start</code>. <code>start</code> and
  <code>end</code> follow the writing direction, so <code>end-start</code> opens to the right in
  left-to-right pages and to the left in right-to-left pages; submenus open this way. The menu flips and
  shifts to stay in the viewport. <code>offset</code> sets the gap in pixels (default <code>4</code>).
</p>

<h3>Deprecated</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    The physical sides <code>left</code> and <code>right</code> (with or without an alignment): use
    <code>start</code> and <code>end</code>. They still work and log one warning.
  </li>
</ul>
